{"type":"proposition","type_name":"Proposition","number":"2.6.1","title":"Greatest and Least Elements Are Unique","title_html":"Greatest and Least Elements Are Unique","html":"<p>A subset <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"A\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> of a partially\nordered set has at most one greatest element and at most one least\nelement.</p>","file":"ch02-relations-and-induction/06-orders.html"}